coverage:
I read the whole 9.8k-line paper in build/sections/ to see how it is put together. I checked these parts line by line and recomputed the constants:

(1) Introduction and how the main theorem follows from the base-graph theorem plus the matrix obstruction, including the fractional-colouring and kappa corollaries.

(2) matrix-trees.tex in full:
- the hyperboloid and flat normalization bound;
- the finite tree approximation, re-derived (radial identity, error 4, bottleneck log(l-1) bound, K(l));
- the segment-comparison 11K bound;
- the finite tree principle (bags, subdivision count);
- the single-bag sink argument (3q);
- the weighted centroid bag (K_a, c=1/(40K_a), the 11k/5 count and k > 5m/44);
- the common-bag path argument (5q, cm/2, cm/3).

(3) matrix-rank.tex in full:
- the M-matrix lemma;
- the spectral-support lemma (odd moments, the atom at 1, the 2*delta bound);
- the coordinate-matching lemma, every constant re-derived (2tau^2, 6/7, 8tau^2/7, the 5tau^2 and 8tau^2 totals);
- the trace-cross lemma;
- the whole proof of the theorem:
  - discarding negative clique blocks (<2q);
  - d_s >= (1-delta)v;
  - indefinite-group weight < m/10;
  - candidate weight > 3m/10;
  - the smallness inequalities from delta_0 and beta_0;
  - p/v >= 1/2 - 3tau^2 and t/v >= c/3;
  - the sign domination |<R,Q>| <= -<H,Q>;
  - the exact complement L_e;
  - Tr E = t giving k_s >= t/3;
  - the joint positive-index count 1/2 + c/9 - 64tau - (275/49)tau^2 >= 1/2 + c/12.

(4) 02-geometry: the parity-sum proof that the hole relation is triangle-free (so alpha <= 2), and the cut-kernel lemma.

(5) 03-distributions:
- the frame-orbit and image-cap lemmas;
- the channel-thinning concentration (influence bounds, tail versus p^{k_h}, density 4p^{-2k_h} <= 2^{eps_ch N});
- the raw-intersection sparsity counts (g^2/4 > 2D, z <= 4D/g, 8D/g < g);
- the peeling rank comparison;
- the Walsh estimates.

(6) 06-collision in full: pruning loss 2|K|L_n tau_n, cell p_max 2^{-.95tN}, the character bound 2^{-.45tN}, and the exponent k_max+.03 < 100g.

(7) 13-graph-transfer in full:
- the entropy-increase lemma;
- the resource-price separation;
- the coloured and uncoloured covers;
- the fingerprint count exp(O(N^3 2^{100gN})) = exp(o(m));
- the tail bounds;
- the derivation of (G1)-(G3), including 8am/eta < m/100 and the maximal-matching step for (G3).

(8) Final propositions of 12-status-span and 12b-asymmetric (coloured and asymmetric tests, 44g+55.97 margin, eta_col < c_*/4), and the parameter ledger in section 14 for ordering consistency.

NOT verified in depth: the long probabilistic overlap core, i.e. sections 04 moments, 05 realization beyond the recipe lemma, 07 phases, 08 preparation, 09 histograms, 10 product tests, 11 common limit, most of 12/12b, and 15 measures. I only spot-checked these; I found nothing wrong in them, but this does not certify them.
